# Short, tappable entry points for the links we TEXT people.
#
# Two constraints collide in an SMS: US carriers block "https://…netlify.app/?…"
# outright (error 30007), and phones won't linkify a bare ".app" domain that
# carries a query string. A clean path clears both — written bare it survives the
# carrier filter, and iOS/Android turn it into a tappable link.
#
# 302, NOT a 200 rewrite: the app reads ?mode from the browser's own URL, so the
# browser has to actually land on /?mode=… A rewrite would leave location.search
# empty and drop the visitor on the homeowner intake page instead.
/timecard   /?mode=timecard   302
/checkin    /?mode=timecard&checkin=1   302
/payroll    /?mode=payroll    302
